# Chess knowledge pack - relation vocabulary (lesson 00)
#
# Defines every verb used in this domain so the engine knows
# which questions become askable.
#
# Standard relations (already in demo):
#   is a          -> taxonomy / class membership
#   is_part_of    -> part-whole (transitive)
#   shows         -> property / observable attribute
#
# Chess-specific relations:
#   can_move_like      -> how a piece moves (its movement pattern)
#   can_capture_like   -> how a piece captures (often same as move)
#   starts_on          -> starting square or zone on the board
#   has_count          -> number of this piece per side
#   is_played_on       -> which surface/object the game uses
#   wins_by            -> how a side wins the game

# -- bootstrap examples for each relation --
chess is a board_game
a_chessboard is_part_of chess
chess shows strategy
the_king can_move_like one_square_in_any_direction
the_queen can_capture_like any_direction_unlimited_squares
the_king starts_on e1_or_e8
the_king has_count one_per_side
chess is_played_on a_chessboard
chess wins_by checkmating_the_opponent_king
